Subject: Fix: the goalie's sweep test sees the ball as near on every platform
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

A fix of the original game, always on and without a switch. It lives in the
tweak series so the faithful series stays retail.

PhysicsGoalie::IsBallNearGoalie, the first part of the sweep test that
catches a ball going through a goalie between two steps, widens the goalie's
reach by ballMaxMotionPerTick: a global PhysicsGoalie.cpp initialises at
startup from FixedUpdateTask::GetPhysicsUpdateTick(), that is from
g_fSimulationTick, which FixedUpdateTask.cpp initialises at startup as well.
The order of two files' initialisations is the linker's: with
PhysicsGoalie.cpp first, the tick is still zero and the reach stays 0
instead of 1.8. The Linux build initialises them in one order and the
Windows build in the other, so a network match between them diverged as soon
as a ball passed within 1.8 of a goalie's reach (found with the rollback's
desync fields: the same inputs gave the test 1 on one machine, 0 on the
other). The test now takes the fixed tick, a constant set before any
initialisation runs: 1.8 on every platform, the value its formula means.

diff --git a/src/Game/Physics/PhysicsGoalie.cpp b/src/Game/Physics/PhysicsGoalie.cpp
index 1ce173f..f0adbb4 100644
--- a/src/Game/Physics/PhysicsGoalie.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Physics/PhysicsGoalie.cpp
@@ -84,6 +84,21 @@ bool PhysicsGoalie::IsBallNearGoalie(float goalieRadius,
 
     nlVector3 diff;
     nlVec3Sub(diff, ballPrevPosition, goaliePos);
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Port fix, always on: ballMaxMotionPerTick is a global initialised at
+    // startup from g_fSimulationTick, another file's global initialised at
+    // startup too. C++ leaves the order of the two to the linker: where this
+    // file goes first it reads the tick while still zero and keeps 0 instead
+    // of 1.8 (90 m/s for 0.02 s), and the goalie's sweep test misses balls
+    // the other platforms catch. The fixed tick is a constant, set before any
+    // file's initialisation runs.
+    return (nlVec3Length(diff)
+               - (goalieRadius
+                   + (ballRadius
+                       + PhysicsBall::GetBallMaxVelocity()
+                           * g_fFixedUpdateTick)))
+        <= 0.0f;
+#endif
     return (nlVec3Length(diff)
                - (goalieRadius + (ballRadius + ballMaxMotionPerTick)))
         <= 0.0f;
